<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-INGRESS-ADMIT-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-INGRESS-ADMIT-001" ;
  triage:title "Local HTTP ingress on the replacement runtime fails admission under the official send benchmark: uds, tcp and tcp-tls lanes fail at f1 to f16 on 1.4.10 (accepted 1 of 1000, 95 rows persisted, connection closed before response headers); tcp on 1.4.9 admitted 600 of 1000 with HTTP 503 receiver-endpoint lookup failures" ;
  triage:description "Release-readiness step 1 on rand-m5/atmbench. Candidate 1.4.10 @ eefa01418 (campaign 20260903T185218Z-m5-atmbench, PR #1147): the sqlite lane PASSes (p50 43893.46 msg/s) but the first network lane, direct-v4 UDS f8 (raw trace 20260903-185252.408800-m5-atmbench-uds-f8.json on atmbench), records metrics requested_count=1000, accepted_count=1, durability_after_restart observed_mailbox_count=95 with expected_accepted_count=1 and durability passed=false; the first failure is that the daemon closed the local HTTP connection before response headers. The per-target diagnostic sweep on the same build shows UDS f1/f2/f4/f8 FAIL and f16/f64 PASS, TCP f1..f16 FAIL and f64 PASS, TCP-TLS f1..f16 FAIL and f64 PASS, each reported only as FAIL admission-capacity evidence with no reason text. Candidate 1.4.9 @ 2e3c93a7c (campaign 20260903T183628Z, PR #1146) already showed the tcp lane at p50 422.18 msg/s with messages_admitted=600 of 1000 and first_failure HTTP 503 ATM_MAILBOX_WRITE_FAILED failed to look up graft receiver endpoint (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/graft_receiver_endpoint_store.rs:211); uds and tcp-tls could not run on 1.4.9 because of RRG-BENCH-FQDN-001. Classification: product, blocking, against the replacement runtime local ingress (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs canonical write path around line 886, where local writes still await emit_received_hook before responding) and the graft receiver endpoint lookup that the hook performs; NOT the frozen legacy synchronous daemon. The mailbox holding 95 rows while only 1 admission was acknowledged means writes are persisted and then the response is lost or the connection is dropped, so the admission accounting seen by the client disagrees with durable state. Whether a1d4783c7 (peer-ingress hook detachment) changed local-path behaviour must be checked by rerunning uds f8 at 50e8614f9 versus a1d4783c7; the 1.4.9 tcp 503 evidence predates that commit, so the endpoint-lookup failure is at least partly pre-existing. Fix must land in atm-http-runtime or its storage adapters and be proven by a focused uds/tcp f8 rerun on atmbench before the full campaign. Fix round 3 (c1e521aa4: bounded idle pool for SharedDb control-path connections, bounded-backoff accept recovery) partially resolved it: focused uds f8 rerun on atmbench at c7f0fe7ec (2026-09-04T02:48Z, raw trace 20260904-024853.637104-local-uds-f8.json on atmbench) shows accepted_count equals durable rows equals 639 of 1000, so the closed-before-response-headers symptom and the accounting disagreement are gone, but 361 requests still received HTTP 503 ATM_MAILBOX_WRITE_FAILED during graft receiver endpoint lookup. Record stays open; residual mechanism (busy handling on control-path connections, effective concurrency bound, or the daemon RLIMIT_NOFILE soft limit under launchd) under root-cause on the same branch. Focused tcp f8 on the same commit (2026-09-04T02:49Z) also failed: accepted equals durable equals 662 of 1000, 338 HTTP 503 ATM_MAILBOX_WRITE_FAILED, first failure reported as failed to open SQLite database, which points at connection-open exhaustion under load rather than lock contention alone. Fix round 4 pushed as 9ed5b7dd1 (2026-09-04T03:2xZ): root cause is that ControlPathConnections bounded idle rather than live SQLite connections, so descriptor demand scaled with in-flight admissions and hit SQLITE_CANTOPEN extended code 14 (unable to open database file) under the launchd 256-fd soft limit; the endpoint-lookup message is the same code raised lazily at first read on the wal and shm sidecars, the tcp open-failure message is the same code at Connection open. Fix: new control_path_pool bounds live control-path connections at 8 with a Condvar wait bounded by the busy timeout and a RAII lease, plus descriptor_limit raise at HttpRuntime start as defence in depth. Local proof under ulimit -n 256: pre-fix 48 failures at concurrency 128 and 3034 at 160; post-fix 0 failures up to concurrency 256 with 38 to 42 fds peak. Regression tests in control_path_pool and descriptor_limit; just lint and just test exit 0. Awaiting focused uds and tcp f8 rerun on atmbench. Live proof on 9ed5b7dd1 (atmbench, 2026-09-04T03:14Z to 03:15Z, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 BENCH GO): focused uds f8 PASS, requested equals accepted equals durable equals 116000, no first failure, evidence 20260904-031403.388389-local-uds-f8.json; focused tcp f8 PASS, requested equals accepted equals durable equals 108000, no first failure, evidence 20260904-031452.110312-local-tcp-f8.json. Full step 1 (smoke, benchmark-official, benchmark-read) and the evidence PR follow under a separate BENCH GO. Closure verdict is quality-mgr's. Re-scope at QA-4c (arch-qa ARCH-002, 2026-09-04): occurrence CAND-1 (local-ingress writes await emit_received_hook inline before responding) is a distinct mechanism untouched by fix rounds 3 and 4 and is now tracked by RRG-INGRESS-LOCAL-HOOK-AWAIT-001 (important); this record covers only the descriptor-exhaustion mechanism (CAND-2, CAND-3) and its closure does not claim CAND-1. Full step 1 official benchmark at f5de13551 (campaign 20260904T033320Z-m5-atmbench, 2026-09-04T03:33Z to 03:4xZ, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 GO): admission is now correct on every lane (sqlite 924000 of 924000, uds 117000 of 117000, tcp 108000 of 108000, tcp-tls 145000 of 145000) but throughput FAILS the floors on all three network lanes: sqlite p50 48238.36 PASS; uds p50 6105.66 vs floor 18000; tcp p50 5523.52 vs floor 17000; tcp-tls p50 7371.04 vs floor 13500. Fix round 4 traded admission failures for a roughly three-fold throughput regression, so the record stays open and blocking; fix round 5 on the same branch must recover the floors without regressing admission (rule: no fix may regress numbers already hit). Prime suspect is the fix round 4 control_path_pool bound of 8 live connections with Condvar waiting on the blocking pool serialising endpoint lookups and the inline local received-hook await (RRG-INGRESS-LOCAL-HOOK-AWAIT-001) sitting inside that critical path; root cause to be established, not assumed. Evidence commit 257b39112 retained on atmbench; automatic push failed because the evidence branch name differs from the requested chore branch, evidence PR to follow. Occurrence CAND-4 records the regression at f5de13551. QA-4c/5 update 2026-09-04T03:41Z (quality-mgr): evidence PR for the FAIL campaign 20260904T033320Z at f5de13551 is https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1149 (develop base, same shape as #1147), recorded against occurrence CAND-4. Closure still waits on the fix-round-5 rerun evidence; QA-5 will run once arch-ctm pushes r5. Fix round 5 (3a9aa54d5: MAX_CONTROL_PATH_CONNECTIONS raised from 8 to 64 plus a 64-borrow regression test) DISPROVEN live: focused runs on atmbench at 3a9aa54d5 (2026-09-04T03:53Z to 03:54Z, arch-ctm under fenix@rand-m5 focused GO) keep admission exact but drop throughput further: uds f8 p50 951.29 with accepted equal to durable equal to 18000 (evidence 20260904-035352.614851-local-uds-f8.json), tcp f8 p50 867.15 with 19000 (evidence 20260904-035431.426670-local-tcp-f8.json), no first failure. The r4 focused runs at 9ed5b7dd1 moved about 116000 messages in the same duration-bounded window, consistent with the official 6105 per second, so the wider bound made the control path roughly six times slower, which points at SQLite lock or busy-handler contention between control-path connections rather than a descriptor or queueing limit. The pool bound is therefore not the root cause of the gap to the floors; the floors (uds 18000, tcp 17000, tcp-tls 13500) were set on the AO2 replacement-runtime baseline before the graft receiver endpoint lookup and received-hook work landed on develop, and no network lane on this candidate has ever met them, so the regression window is the AO2 baseline to this branch, not only the candidate commits. Fix round 6 must root-cause by measurement (bisect on atmbench focused uds f8, including the AO2 baseline commit and the candidate merge-base with develop) before any further code change, and must not ship 3a9aa54d5 as is because it regresses the r4 number. Amendment v10 (2026-09-04T04:0xZ, team-lead ruling relayed via fenix@rand-m5): the r5 verdict above is downgraded from disproven to INCONCLUSIVE because the r5 focused runs were short (18000 and 19000 requests) versus the f5de13551 baseline (117000 and 108000) and cold-start or warmup skew cannot be excluded. A matched-length rerun at 3a9aa54d5 (about 100000 sustained per lane, uds f8 then tcp f8) is in progress on atmbench under a focused GO from fenix@rand-m5; its result decides r5. If it meets the floors, 3a9aa54d5 stands and the r6 bisect is cancelled; if it does not, the r6 measurement-first bisect proceeds and 3a9aa54d5 is superseded. No further code change lands before that result." ;
  triage:phaseId "readiness-1.4" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "cross-host-transport" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
